    (property "Note" "LIT = THE LOAD SWITCH IS DELIVERING. It hangs on UMBILICAL_POS12, the LT1641 output, so it is dark with the toggle off and dark when the -1 has latched on a fault - the one indication the latching design needs. It does not say the instrument is plugged in. PANEL-MOUNTED (ADR 0024 point 16): no footprint on the board - its leads are cut short and soldered to CBL-LED-PANEL, the lead that plugs into J-LED-PANEL, anode to pin 1" (at 91.44 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Pins_source" "datasheets/led/DIALIGHT-605-SERIES-PMI-CATALOG-2021-EXCERPT.pdf p.1: 'Anode (Dot)' - the anode lead is the one the dot on the housing's back marks. A stand-in pin map: the LED is on the panel, and its pins are its two leads as the lead reaches them" (at 91.44 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "Manufacturer" "Dialight" (at 91.44 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
    (property "MPN" "605-2211-110F" (at 91.44 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
